# Scheduled class periods. Attendance is reported per session rather than per
# calendar day, so a laptop that happens to be near the router at 9am does not
# turn into an attendance record.
#
#   name|days|start|end
#
# days   comma-separated, mon tue wed thu fri sat sun
# start  24-hour local time, HH:MM
# end    24-hour local time; SESSION_BUFFER_MIN in classnet.conf is added to it,
#        so students who linger a few minutes still count as present
#
# Sections may overlap in time; a student is reported under every session whose
# window they were connected for. Times are the router's local time, so set the
# router's timezone (install.sh does this).
#
# Install as /etc/classnet/schedule.conf.

lec-1|tue,thu|08:00|09:45
lec-2|tue,thu|14:40|16:25
lab-1|fri|13:00|14:30
lab-2|fri|14:40|16:10
